cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper and this archive."
title: "k2m5-family: certificates, checkers, Lean proof and paper for s(k^2-5)=k, k>=7"
type: software
version: "1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-14"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/moh63-dev/k2m5-family"
authors:
  - family-names: Khalili
    given-names: Mohsen
  - family-names: Gharabaghi
    given-names: Sara
abstract: "We prove s(k^2-5)=k for every integer k>=7, where s(n) is the side of the smallest square that contains n unit squares with disjoint interiors, rotations allowed. The cases k=7,8,9 are known certificates; for all k>=10 one family of weighted measures on [0,k]^2 (corner module, periodic wall pattern, Lebesgue middle; total mass k^2-4D with D=1.3405...>5/4) is shown valid by reducing, through a locality lemma, to a single 11x11 board, which is checked with Daniel's interval checker zmx2 and a new Tight-Tile Lemma. This archive holds the certificate, the checkers, the Lean reduction, the Tight-Tile checker and its outputs, and the paper."
keywords:
  - square packing
  - unit squares
  - weighted cover
  - interval arithmetic
  - Lean 4
